# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real genealogy data must not reach a public repository.
#
# Genealogy files describe living people. Public tests run on a wholly invented corpus in
# tests/fixtures/; anything real stays local, ignored, under tests/private/. A fixture committed
# once stays in git history even after it is deleted, so this is a gate, not a preference.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/private/
*.private.ged
*.private.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local editor and assistant tooling state.
#
# These files are personal to whoever ran the tool, they churn constantly, and they routinely
# contain absolute paths, file contents and pasted secrets. None of that belongs in a public
# repository. Grouped by vendor so an entry can be un-ignored deliberately with a `!` negation
# next to its group rather than deleting the whole block.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Anthropic -- Claude Code, Claude Desktop
.claude/
.claude.json
.claude.local.json
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.anthropic/

